[00:07.12] [Chorus]
[00:07.12] Well I'm proud to be a hippie from Olema
[00:12.00] Where we're friendly to the squares and all the straights
[00:20.52] We still take in strangers if they're ragged
[00:26.26] We can't think of anyone to hate
[00:32.92] [Verse 1]
[00:33.76] We don't watch commercials in Olema
[00:38.38] We don't buy the plastic crap they sell
[00:46.32] We still wear our hair long like folks used to
[00:52.90] And we bathe often, therefore we don't smell
[00:57.96] [Chorus]
[00:58.74] [Verse 2]
[00:59.16] We don't throw our beer cans on the highway
[01:05.84] We don't slight a man because he's black
[01:05.96] We don't spill our oil out in the ocean
[01:05.96] 'Cause we love birds and fish too much for that
[01:05.96] [Alternate Chorus]
[01:05.96] And I'm proud to be a hippie from Olema
[01:05.96] Where we're friendly to the squares and all the straights
[01:11.00] We still take in strangers if they're Haggard
